That depends on how animals were selected for telemetry and other details of the particular study. Are you intending to collect new data? There are some downsides: in general there is little direct benefit from including telemetry, you must make additional assumptions, and 'secr' is overdue for an overhaul in this area. The indirect benefit of telemetry is that it informs model choice - it's always good to have a feeling for how your animal behaves (home range shape, behaviour at barriers, heterogeneity etc.).
Murray

