I suppose so, but I think my comment stands. Cobbling together datasets, with sigma informed only by telemetry, is sensible in extreme cases. It does assume that the telemetry sigma is the same as the detection sigma, and that you have telemetered an unbiased sample of the population. This seems likely to involve handwaving and pleas for forgiveness, which again is fine in extreme cases (Florida panthers?).
Murray

