In most cases, telemetry contributes only to the estimate of sigma (not g0 or lambda0). You can assess the potential benefit from external (telemetry) estimation of sigma by fixing the value of sigma when fitting an SECR model to plain (e.g. cameras-only) data. If you have at least a modest number of recaptures then the precision of estimated density won't change much. For example, if your preliminary estimate of sigma is 3km
secr.fit(CH, fixed = list(sigma = 3000))

Murray

